# NIZAM - what never enters an image build context.
#
# Owning contract: PFOS 12 - Two-Agent VPS Deployment & Operations. Spec task 10.8, requirement R24.
# Companion: ops/IMAGE_BUILD.md, and the two image recipes under ops/images/.
#
# THE FIRST BLOCK IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS. A build context is a copy of this directory handed to the
# builder, so a broad COPY can put a private key inside a layer that is then tagged, pushed, and
# unreadable-once-shipped. Nothing below is a size optimization; the untracked secret material and
# the local environment files are excluded first, by name and by directory, so a future COPY of a
# whole subtree cannot pick one up by accident. Being gitignored does not help here - the builder
# does not read .gitignore.
.secrets/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
ops/env/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_rsa*

# Version control and editor state. A .git directory in a context is both large and a full history
# of every file that was ever in it, including one that was removed for a reason.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode/
.kiro/

# Installed and generated trees. Dependencies are resolved inside the build from the lockfile so the
# result does not depend on this machine, and dist/ is the browser bundle, which no server image runs.
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.loop/
.vite/

# Local data and research. Real ledgers are gitignored and must never reach an image either.
data/ledgers/*.json
docs/research/
outputs/
